#: ../../run.md:217
msgid "Using the Recorder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:219
msgid "The Recorder is a tool used to save a bunch of transactions in a JSON file and re-run them later, either in the same environment or in another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:222
msgid "Saving to the JSON file (by default it's called scenario.json) allows one to easily check the transaction list, tweak input parameters, change linked libraries, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:224
msgid "There are many use cases for the Recorder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:226
msgid "For instance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:228
msgid "After having coded and tested contracts in a constrained environment, like the Remix VM, you could then switch the environment and redeploy the contract to a more realistic environment, like a public testnet or to a Geth node. By using the generated **scenario.json** file, you will be using all the same settings that you used in the Remix VM. And, this means that you won't need to click the interface 100 times or whatever to get the state that you achieved originally. Thus the Recorder can be a tool to protect your sanity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:231
msgid "You can also change the settings in the scenario.json file to customize the playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:233
msgid "Deploying a contract often requires more than creating one transaction, and the Recorder will automate this deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:236
msgid "Working in a dev environment often requires setting up the state initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:239
msgid "![The Recorder panel showing the transactions recorded count and save button.](images/deploy-and-run/recorder.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:239
msgid "The Recorder panel showing the transactions recorded count and save button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:241
msgid "When checked, the option `Run transactions using the last compilation result` allows you to develop a contract and easily set the state using **the latest compiled versions of the contracts.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:243
msgid "scenario.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:245
msgid "To create this file in the Recorder, you first need to have run some transactions. In the image above, it shows a `0` next to **Transactions Recorded**. So, this isn't the right moment to save transactions because, well, because there aren't any. But, each time you make a transaction, that number will increment. So, when you are ready with some transactions, click the floppy disk icon and the scenario.json file will be created."
msgstr ""

